-- The front matter (title, important notice, table of contents) and Part II, Articles 1-3:
-- the contract, its period and premium, and how it ends. Quotations (`src:N`) are generated
-- from line N of ../../source/raw/baoviet-vcx-2021.txt.
--
-- DAYS. Where these Articles count "ngày" the Rules do not say calendar or working days;
-- where they mean working days they say so (4.2.7, 5.2.4). So a bare "day" is read as a
-- calendar day (fork F6). A period of N days "from" a date is read as ending N days after
-- that date: the day of the event is not counted (fork F7). That is the Civil Code's rule
-- for periods in days as this encoder understands it (outside knowledge, unverified).

