-- The notice makes the purchaser's signature on the request form, or the electronic
-- confirmation or OTP, evidence that the purchaser understood the whole of the Rules.
-- LAW: Article 19(2) of the Law on Insurance Business (aid, lines 435-440) puts on the
-- insurer a duty to explain the exclusions and to hold evidence that it did. Whether a
-- signature on a form that says "you have understood" is that evidence is not something
-- the Rules can settle (fork F3, finding X12).
@ref Rules, important notice (src 7-12); Part I definition 6 (src 63-68)
GIVEN `the policy` IS A `The policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice — the purchaser is taken to have understood the whole of the Rules` `the policy` MEANS
    `the request counts as signed under definition 6` `the policy`

